derivations.claim:
(Killing contraction.) Write $T^{ab}
abla_a\xi_b=	frac12T^{ab}(
abla_a\xi_b+
abla_b\xi_a)+	frac12T^{ab}(
abla_a\xi_b-
abla_b\xi_a)$. The first summand vanishes by the Killing equation. In the second, the symmetry $T^{ab}=T^{ba}$ and a relabelling $a\leftrightarrow b$ give $T^{ab}(
abla_a\xi_b-
abla_b\xi_a)=T^{ab}
abla_a\xi_b-T^{ba}
abla_a\xi_b=0$. Hence $T^{ab}
abla_a\xi_b=0$. This proves (d).

(The divergence source.) Using the product formula and step 1.1, $T^{ab}
abla_an_b=	frac1XT^{ab}
abla_a\xi_b-T^{ab}n_ba_a$; the first term vanishes by [L5], and the second is $-(T^{ab}n_b)a_a=J^aa_a$ by [L4]. Since $a$ is spatial and $\Phi=J-\mu n$, $J^aa_a=\Phi^aa_a+\mu n^aa_a=\Phi^aa_a$ by [L6] and clause (a) of [[lem-gr-congruence-acceleration-and-expansion-properties]]. Substituting into [L5] gives $
abla_aJ^a=-\Phi^aa_a$. This proves (c).

(The source term.) By [L6], $T^{ab}
abla_an_b=(\varepsilon+p)n^an^b
abla_an_b+pg^{ab}
abla_an_b=0+p	heta$ by [L4], where the first term vanishes because $n^b
abla_an_b=0$.
